{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> D::NodeId;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** `Criterion::source_node_id` must return the node the criterion is evaluated on, as a `D::NodeId`. That node is the criterion's source node.\n\n**Tests that check it:**\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` calls the trait method directly. It asserts `review().source_node_id() == node`. The `Review` criterion is built from a specific `HabeasNode::Requirement(\"requirements.ready\")`, and its `source_node_id` returns `self.node.clone()`. A constant or wrong node would fail this assertion. The test also runs the criterion through `verify`, `store_evidence`, and `load_evidence`, which are keyed by that node.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` verifies through the validator. It asserts that the fingerprinted value's `source_node_id()` equals `&Node(1)`, the node the test's `Review` criterion was built with. It asserts that the loaded record's `source_node_id()` equals the stored value's. The `Review` criterion's `source_node_id` returns `self.source.clone()`. This checks that the criterion's declared node is the one the answer is attributed to and persisted under.\n\n**Coverage.** The requirement is a single signature with one obligation: identify the source node. Both tests have `{test}` references to `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.source_node_id`. The assertions check concrete values rather than only executing the code. The requirement names no other boundary, failure case, or mode. Tracked reads of other nodes appear in the `source_node` definition, but they are not an obligation of this requirement.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none, and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
